title: The Nationalist Right
new-page: true
view-if: crisis = 0 and congress = 0 and c_far_right_timer <= 0 and time >= 3
on-arrival: {!
Q.c_far_right_timer = 4;
Q.month_actions += 1;
Q.c_far_right_out = 0;
// the right marches where we are strongest in the streets
RG.target('guards');
!}
frequency: 200
is-card: true
tags: germany

= The Nationalist Right

[? if year <= 1920 : The Freikorps officers who murdered Luxemburg and Liebknecht are heroes in the officers' clubs, and industrialists pay for posters of Bolsheviks with knives in their teeth. ?][? if year >= 1921 and year <= 1922 : The Freikorps have gone underground into rifle clubs and labour companies, and the killers of Organisation Consul pick off the Republic's ministers one by one. ?][? if year >= 1923 : In Munich, a former corporal named Adolf Hitler fills the beer halls, and his storm troopers break up workers' meetings across Bavaria. ?]

This month they marched through a workers' district of **[+ sys_target_name +]**, and a comrade was beaten half to death.

- @break_up: Break up their next meeting.
- @joint: Form defence committees with the social democrats.
- @expose: Publish the names of their paymasters.
- @easy_discard

@break_up
subtitle: The red guards of [+ sys_target_name +] drive them off the streets there, and the police arrest our side.
on-arrival: {!
RG.district(Q.sys_target, {militancy: 6, repression: 6, guards: 0.4});
Q.red_guards_loyalty += 4;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

Our young workers fill the front rows of the next nationalist meeting. It ends after ten minutes, in the street.

@joint
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Workers of every party guard each other's halls.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids any deal with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.spd_relation += 6;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

The SPD's hall stewards had no use for us yesterday. Today they stand at the same door when the nationalists come.

@expose
subtitle: If our information holds, the government is shamed. If it does not, we face a libel suit. The editors think it is even odds.
on-arrival: {!
if (Math.random() < 0.5) {
    Q.c_far_right_out = 1;
    Q.stability -= 3;
    Q.worker_support += 3;
    RG.news('Communists name the industrialists who pay the nationalist leagues', 2);
} else {
    Q.c_far_right_out = 2;
    Q.resources = Math.max(0, Q.resources - 1);
}
!}

[? if c_far_right_out = 1 : Die Rote Fahne prints the list of firms that pay the leagues, with the cheque numbers. The government promises an inquiry. ?][? if c_far_right_out = 2 : Two of the names are wrong. The court fines the paper, and the leagues have their own headline for a week. ?]
